+    // fields shimmer by half a line. While the display keeps alternating between two such buffers,
+    // weave the newest two fields into one full-height frame, the way a TV shows them. The two fields
+    // can come from different game frames (the runtime's vsync is paced by guest frames when they are
+    // slow), so the weave is motion adaptive: a pixel of the older field is kept where neither field
+    // changed since its previous frame, or where it fits between its vertical neighbours; elsewhere
